        "reference": "Psalms 66:12",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "I will go into thy house with burnt offerings: I will pay thee my vows,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:13",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Which my lips have uttered, and my mouth hath spoken, when I was in trouble.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:14",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "I will offer unto thee burnt sacrifices of fatlings, with the incense of rams; I will offer bullocks with goats. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:15",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Come and hear, all ye that fear God, and I will declare what he hath done for my soul.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:16",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "I cried unto him with my mouth, and he was extolled with my tongue.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:17",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "If I regard iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear me:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "Prov. 1:28 (24–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:18",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "But verily God hath heard me; he hath attended to the voice of my prayer.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 66:19",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 66,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Blessed be God, which hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
